scene__
  @name "ACT1: Red Keep Intrigue"
  @first "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @sections "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "The Wall War Map against old law" "Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky" "Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse" "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors" "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower" "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow" "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn" "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain" "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain" "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast" "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell" "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses" "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners" "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery" "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light" "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals" "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries" "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "The Wall War Map against old law"
__scene

section__
  @title "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/01-act1-court/frame-049.jpg"

  "In a shuttered council room, ink pools beside half-burned dispatches while guards listen through the oak door. Varys urges immediate action on a legal ultimatum designed to strip toll and route control, while Grand Maester Pycelle measures whether your hesitation can be framed as disloyalty by supper.

Capital politics rewards timing over sincerity. If you move publicly, you gain procedural legitimacy and surrender surprise. If you move through closed channels, you can seize initiative while feeding the narrative that Valehart governs by deniable coercion. Either choice changes who trusts your next decree and who begins quietly funding your replacement.

This is not debate for its own sake. In King's Landing, information control is force projection with better tailoring."

  choice__
    @target "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Table a legal ultimatum designed to strip toll and route control in open council, bind statements to record, and absorb short-term friction for lawful authority."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Resolve a legal ultimatum designed to strip toll and route control through private intermediaries and sealed concessions, gaining initiative while increasing blackmail exposure."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Wall War Map against old law"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 11)
    @action wealth = clampStat(wealth - 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 2, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Spend coin and offshore contacts to accelerate a legal ultimatum designed to strip toll and route control, buying speed at the cost of deeper external influence in court affairs."
  __choice
__section

