section__
  @title "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/01-act1-court/frame-061.jpg"

  "In a narrow records chamber, wax seals pile beside wine cups and knives laid too close to legal briefs. Varys insists you resolve a blackmail ledger that can reorder court alliances before rivals can define it first, while Grand Maester Pycelle studies your pauses for leverage that can be converted into patronage by nightfall.

By this stage of Act 1, court memory is weaponized: each earlier concession is now cited as precedent against you. Public adjudication can protect legitimacy and expose your coalition seams. Covert adjudication can preserve maneuver but strengthens the argument that law in the capital is merely theater over coercion.

What happens in this chamber will be retold at ten tables by dawn, each version designed to move coin, votes, and knives."

  choice__
    @target "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Submit a blackmail ledger that can reorder court alliances to formal hearing, bind testimony on record, and accept political drag to preserve institutional credibility."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Settle a blackmail ledger that can reorder court alliances through back-channel leverage and selective disclosure, buying control now while compounding future blackmail risk."
  __choice
__section

section__
